items) 4 Psychiatry and Behavioral Sci (3 items) 3 Psychology (1 items) 1 Radiation Oncology (2 items) 2 Radiology (1 items) 1 Religious Studies (1 items) 1 Sarafan ChEM-H (0 items) 0 Sociology (2 items) 2 SoM Dean's Office Admin Units (0 items) 0 Statistics (1 items) 1 Surgery (4 items) 4 Theater & Performance Studies (1 items) 1 Urology (5 items) 5 Line Search employment types 7 filter options found Employment Type CE - Clinician Educator (48 items) 48 Non-Tenure Line (Research) (7 items) 7 Non-Tenure Line (Teaching) (2 items) 2 Other (0 items) 0 Policy Institute Fellows (1 items) 1 University Medical Line (42 items) 42 University Tenure Line (56 items) 56 Location Search cities 2 filter options found City Stanford University (123 items) 123 VA Palo Alto Health Care System (VAPAHCS) (3 items) 3 Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Sort by: Last Updated Last Updated: Newest to Oldest Last Updated: Oldest to Newest Title: A-Z Title: Z-A Clinical Assistant Professor, Stanford Dermatology Stanford University, California Dermatology School of Medicine CE - Clinician Educator The Department of Dermatology at Stanford University School of Medicine is seeking board-certified or board-eligible dermatologists to join the faculty as Clinical Assistant Professors in the Clinician Educator line. Read more Assistant, Associate, or full Professor: Division of Vascular Surgery/Cardiovascular Institute and Division of Abdominal Transplantation/Institute for Immunity, Transplantation and Infection Stanford University, California Surgery School of Medicine Non-Tenure Line (Research) University Medical Line University Tenure Line The Department of Surgery, School of Medicine at Stanford University, is seeking to fill two full-time academic positions, one in the Divisions of Vascular Surgery in conjunction with the Cardiovascular Institute, and one in the Division of Abdominal Transplantation in conjunction with the Institute for Immunity, Transplantation and Infection. These faculty positions will be at the Assistant, Associate, or full Professor level (based on the candidate’s qualifications) in the University Tenure Line (UTL), Non-Tenure Line (Research) (NTL-R), or the University Medical Line (UML). We are particularly interested in candidates who have a mix of scholarly activity, teaching, and, if appropriate, clinical care, based on education and experience. The primary location for these positions will be at the Center for Clinical Sciences Research (CCSR). Read more Orthopaedic Hand Surgeon Stanford University, California Orthopaedic Surgery School of Medicine University Medical Line Department of Orthopaedic Surgery at Stanford University seeks a board certified/eligible orthopaedic surgeon specializing in hand to join the department as Assistant, Associate or Professor rank on the University Medical Line (UML). Read more Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor of Biomedical Data Science Stanford University, California School of Medicine University Tenure Line The Department of Biomedical Data Science (DBDS) at the Stanford University School of Medicine (SoM) invites applications for an open-rank faculty position at the Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor level in the University Tenure Line (UTL). We are particularly interested in candidates who develop and apply novel artificial intelligence (AI) and biomedical data science methodologies to advance biomedical discovery and improve clinical care. Read more Assistant Professor of Microbiology & Immunology Stanford University, California School of Medicine University Tenure Line The Department of Microbiology & Immunology at Stanford University seeks applications for a tenure-track faculty position at the Assistant Professor level in the University Tenure Line. We seek outstanding scientist with a doctoral degree whose research addresses fundamental and emerging questions in broadly defined areas of microbiology and/or immunology. Read more Assistant Professor or Associate Professor without Tenure, Management Science and Engineering Stanford University, California Mgmt Science & Engineering School of Engineering University Tenure Line The Department of Management Science and Engineering at Stanford University invites applications for a tenure track faculty position at the junior level (Assistant or untenured Associate Professor) from individuals working at the frontiers of MS&E. MS&E is a multidisciplinary department with research efforts spanning a broad intellectual spectrum, from analytics and computation to the social and behavioral sciences, united by an interest in engineering solutions to pressing societal problems. Please visit our website for more information about the MS&E Department at http://www.stanford.edu/dept/MSandE/. \n\nApplicants must have completed, or be completing, a Ph.D. in the advertised field or a closely related one. Evidence of the ability to pursue a program of research, and a strong commitment to graduate and undergraduate teaching are also required. A successful candidate will be expected to teach courses at the graduate and undergraduate levels and to build and lead a team of graduate students in PhD research. Read more Assistant or Untenured Associate Professor in Chemical Engineering Department Stanford University, California Chemical Engineering School of Engineering University Tenure Line The Department of Chemical Engineering at Stanford University invites applications for a university tenure-track (UTL) faculty position at the junior level (Assistant or untenured Associate Professor). Read more Assistant Professor, Department of Statistics Stanford University, California Statistics School of Humanities & Sciences University Tenure Line The Department of Statistics at Stanford University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in any area of Statistics or Probability. Read more Faculty Position in Early Learning: Mechanisms and Interventions Stanford University, California Graduate School of Education University Tenure Line The Stanford Graduate School of Education seeks a faculty member at the assistant or associate professor level whose research focuses on developing, testing, and studying interventions that support young children’s learning and development.\n\nWe are particularly interested in scholars who conduct theoretically grounded research in applied settings — including homes, schools, early childhood programs, and community contexts — to identify mechanisms of learning and developmental change, evaluate intervention effectiveness, and examine the conditions that support successful implementation.\n\nThis work may draw on implementation science to inform the development, adaptation, and delivery of scalable interventions and enrich developmental science.\n\nResearch areas may span foundational domains of learning and development, including cognition; early mathematics and STEM learning; early language and literacy; social-emotional development; creativity; and related skills that support children’s educational success.\n\nApplicants should focus on learning and development from early childhood through the early elementary years.\n\nPreference will be given to applicants whose research attends to cultural and contextual variation in learning, addresses issues of educational opportunity and equity, and includes children and families from historically underserved communities. Read more Faculty Appointment in Korean Studies Stanford University, California Freeman Spogli Institute for I Dean of Research Non-Tenure Line (Research) Policy Institute Fellows Stanford University seeks candidates for a faculty position in Korean Studies, with a preference for those in social science of contemporary Korea or its international relations. The successful candidate will be expected to advance research and education on Korea, in the Korea Program of the Walter H. Shorenstein Asia-Pacific Research Center (APARC). Read more Pediatric Endocrinology Clinician Educator Stanford University, California Pediatrics School of Medicine CE - Clinician Educator The Division of Endocrinology & Diabetes in the Department of Pediatrics at Stanford University School of Medicine/Stanford Medicine Children’s Health is recruiting a Clinician Educator as a Clinical Assistant Professor, Clinical Associate Professor, or Clinical Professor. The major criterion for appointment as Clinician Educators is excellence in the overall mix of clinical care, teaching, administrative and/or scholarship appropriate to the programmatic need the individual is expected to fulfill. Read more Assistant Professor of Theater and Performance Studies, Open Area Stanford University, California Theater & Performance Studies School of Humanities & Sciences University Tenure Line The Department of Theater and Performance Studies (TAPS) at Stanford University seeks applicants for a tenure-track Assistant Professor. The area of specialization is open.\n\nApplicants should exhibit the potential for excellence in scholarship, teaching, and, where relevant, creative practice, in line with the Department’s mission to train scholar-artists. The successful candidate must have a Ph.D. in a related field by 1 September 2027 and will be expected to teach and advise students at both the graduate and undergraduate levels. The term of appointment is expected to begin on 1 September 2027. Read more Assistant,  Untenured Associate, or Tenured Associate Professor, Aeronautics and Astronautics Stanford University, California Aeronautics & Astronautics School of Engineering University Tenure Line The Department of Aeronautics and Astronautics at Stanford University invites applications for a tenure track faculty position at the Assistant,  untenured Associate, or tenured Associate Professor level. Read more Open Rank Faculty Position - Social Sciences/Humanities of Education in a Rapidly Changing World Stanford University, California Graduate School of Education University Tenure Line The Stanford Graduate School of Education seeks outstanding applicants at any faculty rank for a social scientist or humanities scholar studying fundamental questions about the role of education in contemporary society. Over the last twenty-five years, American society has changed dramatically. We have experienced rapid demographic and geopolitical shifts, rising inequality and polarization, climate-induced disasters, and massive technological innovation. We seek applicants attempting to understand the role of education amidst these societal transformations. We welcome applicants from a range of disciplinary and interdisciplinary spaces, including but not limited to anthropology, economics, education, history, philosophy, political science, psychology, sociology, gender studies, or STS. Research foci may include a wide range of substantive issues related to the societal changes above. The successful candidate will join a productive community of faculty who study educational phenomena from a variety of disciplinary perspectives, many of whom have interests in collaborating with colleagues across the university as well as with practitioners to understand and facilitate change. The successful candidate will also be expected to teach and advise students at the graduate level. Read more Classics and Civics, Senior Rank Faculty Position in Classics Stanford University, California Classics School of Humanities & Sciences University Tenure Line The Department of Classics at Stanford University seeks applicants for a senior appointment at the rank of Associate Professor or Professor. We are looking for a senior scholar (a tenured Associate or Full Professor) whose research profile aligns with key areas of the Stanford Civics Initiative; we are especially interested in scholars of Roman rhetoric and Roman political philosophy. Applicants must have demonstrated a commitment to effective teaching and mentoring and the ability to maintain a world-class research program. The successful candidate must have a Ph.D. in a related field and will be expected to teach and advise students at both the graduate and undergraduate levels. The term of appointment is expected to begin on September 1, 2027. Read more Assistant Professor in Climate Science Stanford University, California Doerr School of Sustainability University Tenure Line Stanford University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor in the field of Climate Science. The home department may be any of the seven departments in the Stanford Doerr School of Sustainability, with the final choice dependent on the preferences of the candidate and the department. The scope of the search is broad, and we welcome applications from scholars studying all aspects of climate science, including climate processes, climate-change impacts, and sustainability engineering. Relevant approaches may be modeling and theoretical studies, laboratory and field work, and synthesis of modern, historical, and satellite data. Read more Senior Rank, History of Political Thought Stanford University, California History School of Humanities & Sciences University Tenure Line The Department of History at Stanford University invites applications for a senior faculty appointment (with tenure) at the rank of Associate Professor or Professor in the history of political thought and institutions, broadly construed. We welcome historians whose research examines (but is not limited to): citizenship and civic belonging; political rights and representation; democracy and its alternatives; revolutions; constitutions and institutions of governance; elections, parties, and political movements; state formation and political economy; publics, media, and political communication; civil society and associational life. We invite applications from scholars working in any time period and region, and encourage candidates whose work brings non-Western, transnational, comparative, or global perspectives. Applicants should have an outstanding record of research and publication, a demonstrated commitment to excellent teaching and mentoring, and the capacity to sustain a world-class research program. The successful candidate will hold a Ph.D. in History or a closely related field and will be expected to teach and advise students at both the undergraduate and graduate levels. The appointment is expected to begin on September 1, 2027. Read more Open Field, Open Rank Faculty Position in Political Science Stanford University, California Political Science School of Humanities & Sciences University Tenure Line The Department of Political Science at Stanford University is seeking applications for a tenure line open rank, open subfield position. Read more American Politics, Senior Rank Faculty Position in Political Science Stanford University, California Political Science School of Humanities & Sciences University Tenure Line The Department of Political Science at Stanford University seeks applicants for a senior appointment at the rank of Associate Professor or Professor. Read more Comparative Politics, Open Rank Faculty Position in Political Science Stanford University, California Political Science School of Humanities & Sciences University Tenure Line The Department of Political Science at Stanford University is seeking applications for an open rank, tenure line position in Comparative Politics. Read more Political Theory/Civic Thought and Practice, Senior Rank Faculty Position in Political Science Stanford University, California Political Science School of Humanities & Sciences University Tenure Line The Department of Political Science at Stanford University seeks applicants for a senior appointment at the rank of Associate Professor or Professor. The preferred area of specialty is Political Theory. Read more Assistant Professor in Chemistry (Open Area) Stanford University, California Chemistry School of Humanities & Sciences University Tenure Line The Department of Chemistry at Stanford University seeks applicants for a tenure-track Assistant Professor in any area of chemistry. Read more Senior Faculty Position in Chemistry (Open Area) Stanford University, California Chemistry School of Humanities & Sciences University Tenure Line The Department of Chemistry at Stanford University seeks applicants for a tenure-track Associate or Full Professor in any area of chemistry. Read more Orthopaedic Pediatric Surgeon – Stanford University Stanford University, California Orthopaedic Surgery School of Medicine CE - Clinician Educator University Medical Line The Department of Orthopaedic Surgery at Stanford University seeks an Assistant Professor, Associate Professor or Professor to join in the University Medical Line (UML) or Clinician Educator (CE) Line as an orthopaedic pediatric surgeon. We are particularly interested in candidates who have interests in foot/ankle, hip deformity and preservation, and sports.  Candidates must be board certified/eligible in orthopaedic surgery and eligible for a California Medical License. Read more Assistant Professor in Islamic Studies Stanford University, California Religious Studies School of Humanities & Sciences University Tenure Line The Department of Religious Studies at Stanford University invites applications for the tenure-track position of Assistant Professor in Islamic Studies. Read more Assistant Professor of Latin American Literature and Cultures, including Brazil Stanford University, California Iberian & Latin Amer Cultures School of Humanities & Sciences University Tenure Line The Department of Iberian and Latin American Cultures (ILAC) at Stanford University invites applications for a tenure-line Assistant Professor in Latin American literature and cultures, including Brazil. Read more Moral, Political, or Social Philosophy - Senior Rank Faculty Position in Philosophy Stanford University, California Philosophy School of Humanities & Sciences University Tenure Line The Department of Philosophy at Stanford University seeks applicants for a senior appointment at the rank of Associate Professor or Professor. The preferred area of specialty is moral, political, or social philosophy. Read more Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor of Health Policy (Health Economist) Stanford University, California Health Policy School of Medicine University Medical Line University Tenure Line The Department of Health Policy at Stanford University seeks a Health Economist to join the Department as Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor in the University Tenure Line or University Medical Line. Read more Assistant Professor in Environmental Social Sciences, Stanford Doerr School of Sustainability (Global Environmental Policy) Stanford University, California Environmental Social Sciences Doerr School of Sustainability University Tenure Line Stanford University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor in the field of Global Environmental Policy within the Department of Environmental Social Sciences. The scope of the search is broad, and we welcome applications from scholars studying environmental policy issues from the perspective of the quantitative social sciences or related fields, including candidates who have completed or will soon complete their PhD in economics, political science, environmental policy, or data science as applied to environmental policy. The successful candidate will serve as faculty within the Department of Environmental Social Sciences, at the Stanford Doerr School of Sustainability. Read more Assistant Professor in Environmental Social Sciences, Stanford Doerr School of Sustainability (Environmental Behavioral Sciences) Stanford University, California Environmental Social Sciences Doerr School of Sustainability University Tenure Line Stanford University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor in the field of Environmental Behavioral Sciences within the Department of Environmental Social Sciences. The scope of the search is broad, and we welcome applications from candidates involved in any aspect of the study of human ecology, human behavior, or human institutions as they pertain to sustainability, climate change, adaptation, or resilience. Our department operates on the principle that addressing environmental challenges requires deciphering the complex behavioral, structural, or historical dynamics of human systems. We seek an innovative scholar focusing at any—or the integration—of these levels, whether investigating individual choices and behavior change, structural dynamics and social organization, the institutional governance of resources and risk, or related topics. We welcome candidates who approach these questions through diverse research strategies—whether qualitative, quantitative, or mixed-methods—including formal and computational modeling, experimental and data-driven analyses, or field-based, systemic, and historical inquiries. Candidates must have a PhD or other terminal doctoral degree in a field relevant to the search, an excellent record of scholarly work, and a dedication to teaching and mentorship.\n\nThe Stanford Doerr School of Sustainability is an interdisciplinary, mission-driven school, and we seek scholars who are comfortable forging collaborations across disciplines and departments. Read more Displaying 31 - 60 of 125 in total ‹ 1 2 3 4 5 › Powered by PageUp Get Help Questions about a job or your application? Find out how to request help Equal Opportunity Stanford is an equal employment opportunity and affirmative action employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Stanford welcomes applications from all who would bring additional dimensions to the University’s research, teaching and clinical missions. Consistent with its obligations under the law, the University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants and employees with disabilities. Applicants requiring a reasonable accommodation for any part of the application or hiring process should contact disability.access@stanford.edu . Stanford University Stanford Home Maps & Directions Search Stanford Emergency Info Terms of Use Cookie Preferences Privacy Copyright Trademarks Non-Discrimination Accessibility © 2026 Stanford University. Stanford, California 94305. Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all"
